### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and IntelliJ HTTP client.
### Run the login request first, the session cookie is reused automatically.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Login (marks the agent available)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "priya", "password": "agent123" }

### Who am I
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me

### Simulate 3 random interactions
POST {{host}}/api/simulator/interactions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "count": 3 }

### Simulate one specific high priority loan call
POST {{host}}/api/simulator/interactions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "count": 1, "skill": "LOAN", "channel": "CALL", "priority": 1, "customerRef": "CUST-1001" }

### Poll the desk: assigned interaction + customer screen pop
GET {{host}}/api/desk/state

### Add a note (replace 1 with the interaction id from the state call)
POST {{host}}/api/desk/interactions/1/notes
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Customer asked about EMI holiday" }

### Close with a disposition
POST {{host}}/api/desk/interactions/1/close
Content-Type: application/json

{ "disposition": "RESOLVED", "note": "Explained the process, sent the form" }

### Go offline / available (not allowed while on an interaction)
POST {{host}}/api/desk/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "OFFLINE" }

### Which CRM adapter is active
GET {{host}}/api/integration/adapter

### Look up a customer through the active adapter
GET {{host}}/api/integration/customers/CUST-1003

### Mock CRM, JSON api
GET {{host}}/mock-crm/customers/CUST-1001
Accept: application/json

### Mock CRM, legacy XML api
GET {{host}}/mock-crm/legacy/customers/CUST-1001
Accept: application/xml

### Reports
GET {{host}}/api/reports/handle-time?days=30

###
GET {{host}}/api/reports/interactions-per-agent?days=30

###
GET {{host}}/api/reports/queue-length

###
GET {{host}}/api/reports/dispositions?days=30

### Logout
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout
